"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1626,"Narrated to us Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala and Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: ""Narrated to us Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id al-Maqbari, from Abu Salama, from Aisha (RA), who said: 'We had a straw mat that we would spread out during the day, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would roll it up at night, then pray upon it. Then a group of Muslims would follow him, praying as he prayed, and he became aware of them, so he said: ""Take on as much of righteous deeds as you can bear; indeed, Allah does not grow weary until you grow weary."" The most beloved of actions to him was that which was persisted in consistently, even if it was small, and when he performed a prayer, he would maintain it consistently.'
This is the narration reported by Abd al-Jabbar. Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman said: ""Some people heard about this practice, so they prayed following his prayer, and he added: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed, I feared that I would be commanded over you with an obligation that you would not be able to fulfill.'"""
1627,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-San'ani. He said: Al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard Humayd, who narrated on the authority of Anas.

And also narrated to us al-San'ani, who narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, who narrated to us Humayd, who said: Anas said:

And also narrated to us Abu Musa, who narrated to us Khalid ibn al-Harith, who narrated to us Humayd, on the authority of Anas—and this is the narration of Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal.

Anas (RA) reported: The Prophet (ﷺ) prayed in one of his apartments. Some Muslims came and prayed in alignment with his prayer. When he perceived their presence, he made his prayer longer. Then he entered the house and prayed as much as Allah willed. Then he came out and did this repeatedly.

When morning came, they said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in alignment with your prayer last night, and we wished to prolong it.""

He (ﷺ) said: **""I did that deliberately.""**

---

**CHAPTER:**"
